The supplied semantics directly supports ordered dictionary keys, `isinstance(..., str)`, and the `islower`/`isupper` predicates. I’m using an explicit one-pass loop so the implementation matches the contract for empty dictionaries, non-string keys, uncased strings, and mixed-case key sets without relying on unsupported dictionary truthiness.
